IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- gdpr-core-2.l4 -- THE NOUNS K2 ADDS TO THE KEEL OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR).
-- Written by K2 (Sonnet 5.5).  DECLARE only: no rule, no constant, no #EVAL, no #ASSERT.
-- It imports gdpr-core.l4 (P1's keel) and never edits it.
-- Source text: the Publications Office consolidated version of 4.5.2016 (it applies the corrigendum
-- of OJ L 127, 23.5.2018, p. 2).  It is a documentation tool with no legal effect; the Official
-- Journal text is authentic.  Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).
--
-- WHAT BELONGS HERE: an enumeration the text itself makes (the personal aspects Art 4(4) names, the
-- consequences Art 4(12) names, the places Art 4(16) points to) that a seat, a test or a later part
-- would otherwise invent twice, and the party and action types of the one regulative rule of K2
-- (Art 4(9)).  Whether a thing is "profiling", "consent" or "a personal data breach" is a rule and
-- lives in gdpr-definitions-2.l4.
--
-- NAMING (PLAN-P1.md section 2): every type and every constructor begins with the label of the
-- provision it comes from.  Nothing here repeats a name of gdpr-core.l4.
-- ============================================================================

§ `Article 4(4): profiling`

-- "to analyse or predict aspects concerning that natural person's performance at work, economic
-- situation, health, personal preferences, interests, reliability, behaviour, location or movements".
-- The list is "in particular", so it is open: the last member stands for any other personal aspect.
DECLARE `Art 4(4) personal aspect` IS ONE OF
    `Art 4(4) performance at work`
    `Art 4(4) economic situation`
    `Art 4(4) health`
    `Art 4(4) personal preferences`
    `Art 4(4) interests`
    `Art 4(4) reliability`
    `Art 4(4) behaviour`
    `Art 4(4) location`
    `Art 4(4) movements`
    `Art 4(4) some other personal aspect`

§ `Article 4(9): the public authorities that receive personal data in a particular inquiry`

-- The one regulative rule of K2 is Art 4(9): "the processing of those data by those public
-- authorities shall be in compliance with the applicable data protection rules".  The text names the
-- party (those public authorities) and the act (processing in compliance); the types are here so that
-- a later part that must refer to the rule can name them.
DECLARE `Art 4(9) party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 4(9) public authority receiving personal data in a particular inquiry`

DECLARE `Art 4(9) action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 4(9) process the data in compliance with the applicable data protection rules according to the purposes of the processing`

§ `Article 4(11): consent`

-- "by which he or she, by a statement or by a clear affirmative action, signifies agreement".  The
-- last member is the way just outside the two the text names (silence, a pre-ticked box, doing nothing).
DECLARE `Art 4(11) how the data subject signifies agreement` IS ONE OF
    `Art 4(11) by a statement`
    `Art 4(11) by a clear affirmative action`
    `Art 4(11) in some other way, with no statement and no clear affirmative action`

§ `Article 4(12): personal data breach`

-- "a breach of security leading to the accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration,
-- unauthorised disclosure of, or access to, personal data".  "Accidental or unlawful" qualifies
-- destruction, loss and alteration; "unauthorised" qualifies disclosure and access.  The last member
-- is a consequence the definition does not name (for example a delay in processing).
DECLARE `Art 4(12) consequence of a breach of security` IS ONE OF
    `Art 4(12) accidental destruction of personal data`
    `Art 4(12) unlawful destruction of personal data`
    `Art 4(12) accidental loss of personal data`
    `Art 4(12) unlawful loss of personal data`
    `Art 4(12) accidental alteration of personal data`
    `Art 4(12) unlawful alteration of personal data`
    `Art 4(12) unauthorised disclosure of personal data`
    `Art 4(12) unauthorised access to personal data`
    `Art 4(12) some other consequence`

§ `Article 4(16): main establishment`

-- Where the text says the main establishment is: (a) for a controller, the place of its central
-- administration in the Union or, in the exception, the establishment that took the decisions;
-- (b) for a processor, the place of its central administration in the Union or, if it has none in the
-- Union, the establishment in the Union where the main processing activities take place.
DECLARE `Art 4(16) which establishment is the main establishment` IS ONE OF
    `Art 4(16)(a) the place of the controller's central administration in the Union`
    `Art 4(16)(a) the establishment of the controller that took the decisions on the purposes and means`
    `Art 4(16)(b) the place of the processor's central administration in the Union`
    `Art 4(16)(b) the establishment of the processor in the Union where the main processing activities take place`
